stub: {"stubId": "concurrency-14", "topic": "concurrency", "slug": "semaphoreslim-release-without-acquire", "level": "senior", "type": "find-bug", "subtopic": "Locks", "angle": "Shows code using SemaphoreSlim(1, 1) where a method calls Wait(0) and releases in finally even when the wait returned false. A nested call then makes the outer Release throw SemaphoreFullException, and the reader must find the defect.", "answerHinge": "Release must run only when the wait succeeded. Releasing after a failed Wait pushes the count above maxCount, which throws SemaphoreFullException; without a max count it would silently admit extra holders.", "sources": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.threading.semaphoreslim.release", "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.threading.semaphoreslim"]}
Generator notes: Assumes new SemaphoreSlim(1) without an explicit maximum uses int.MaxValue as maxCount, so an extra Release silently raises the count to 2 instead of throwing. This matches the documented constructor behaviour as I recall it but was not re-checked against the page.; Traced output, not run: the original snippet prints 'busy, skipped' and then dies with System.Threading.SemaphoreFullException at the outer Release (line 22). The fixed snippet prints 'busy, skipped' then '1'. Needs run-snippets confirmation.; The local function Save is called recursively and captures the top-level locals gate and saved; I expect this to compile under the statements harness, but it is not verified by a build.
Mechanical evidence:
- executed in the sandbox; declared {"kind": "output", "value": "busy, skipped\n1"}; actual {"kind": "output", "value": "busy, skipped\n1"}
- no mechanical failures
Numbered code.source (quote every line listed in bugLineSets):
  1 | SemaphoreSlim gate = new(1, 1);
  2 | int saved = 0;
  3 | 
  4 | void Save(bool nested)
  5 | {
  6 |     bool acquired = gate.Wait(0);
  7 |     try
  8 |     {
  9 |         if (!acquired)
 10 |         {
 11 |             Console.WriteLine("busy, skipped");
 12 |             return;
 13 |         }
 14 |         if (nested)
 15 |         {
 16 |             Save(false);
 17 |         }
 18 |         saved++;
 19 |     }
 20 |     finally
 21 |     {
 22 |         gate.Release();
 23 |     }
 24 | }
 25 | 
 26 | Save(true);
 27 | Console.WriteLine(saved);
